.TH SDL_GetCurrentRenderOutputSize 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetCurrentRenderOutputSize \- Get the current output size in pixels of a rendering context.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetCurrentRenderOutputSize(SDL_Renderer *renderer, int *w, int *h);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If a rendering target is active, this will return the size of the rendering target in pixels, otherwise return the value of
.BR SDL_GetRenderOutputSize ()\[char46]
.PP
Rendering target or not, the output will be adjusted by the current logical presentation state, dictated by
.BR SDL_SetRenderLogicalPresentation ()\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I renderer
the rendering context\[char46]
.TP
.I w
a pointer filled in with the current width\[char46]
.TP
.I h
a pointer filled in with the current height\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetRenderOutputSize (3)
